<Section collapsed="false" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title>
<Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">4.5 Applications of Congruences</Text-field></Title><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L472" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">In this section we will see how Maple can be used to further explore the applications of congruences discussed in the text.  In particular, we will see how to use a hashing function to store student information in a list.  We will create a pseudorandom number generator.  And we will write a procedure that will check the validity of an ISBN.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L474" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10"><Font bold="true">Hashing Functions</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L987" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The first application we will explore is the hashing function.  Suppose that a small school wants to store information about its students.  In particular, each student has a unique four digit identification number and a GPA, which is a real number between 0 and 4.  </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L989" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10"><Font italic="true">Initial examples</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L475" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Each student record will be stored as a table with indices &quot;ID&quot; and &quot;GPA&quot;.  Here are three example students.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L476" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">student1 := table([&quot;ID&quot;=7319,&quot;GPA&quot;=3.21]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
