<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L480" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Recall that the information in a table can be accessed by enclosing the index in brackets.  For instance, to obtain the GPA of <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">student1</Font>, we issue the following command.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L481" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">student1[&quot;GPA&quot;];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">JCIkQCQhIiM=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L483" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Our student records are going to be stored in a list.  Because the school is small, it will suffice to allocate space for 57 records in the school's database and so we create a list with 57 entries all initialized to 0.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L484" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">studentRecords := [ 0 $ 57 ];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">N2VuIiIhRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGIw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L991" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">In order to store a student record in the list (which represents school's database), we need to apply a hashing function to the unique student ID.  The hashing function we'll use is <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.  Note that the addition of 1 is to occur after the computation of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.  It is included in our function because the indices in our <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords</Font> list run from 1 to 57 while the values of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> range from 0 to 56.  </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L486" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">The following procedure accepts a student ID as input and returns the result of applying the hashing function to the ID number.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L488" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">calculateHash := proc(id::integer)
  return modp(id,57) + 1;
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L490" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">For example,</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L491" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">calculateHash(student1[&quot;ID&quot;]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">IiND</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L493" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">indicates that <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">student1</Font>'s record should be stored in location 24.  We store a record in a particular location in the usual way.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L494" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">studentRecords[24] := student1;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">SSlzdHVkZW50MUc2Ig==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L497" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Note that accessing location 24 returns the table <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">student1</Font>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L498" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">studentRecords[24];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">SSlzdHVkZW50MUc2Ig==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L501" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">To access the ID and GPA stored in location 24, we use a second pair of brackets with the indices &quot;ID&quot; or &quot;GPA&quot;.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L502" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">studentRecords[24][&quot;ID&quot;];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">IiU+dA==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L503" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">studentRecords[24][&quot;GPA&quot;];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">JCIkQCQhIiM=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L505" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">We can store <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">student2</Font>'s information in the same way.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L506" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">calculateHash(student2[&quot;ID&quot;]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">IiIj</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" labelreference="L507" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">studentRecords[2] := student2;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">SSlzdHVkZW50Mkc2Ig==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L509" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">If we try to store <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">student3</Font>'s data, we find that a collision occurs.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L510" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">calculateHash(student3[&quot;ID&quot;]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">IiND</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L512" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Since <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">student3</Font> has the same hash value as <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">student1</Font> did, we look for the next free location.  Check location 25.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L513" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">evalb(studentRecords[25] = 0);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">SSV0cnVlRyUqcHJvdGVjdGVkRw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L515" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Since location 25 is still equal to 0, we know that it has not been used and we store <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">student3</Font>'s record in location 25.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L517" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">studentRecords[25] := student3;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">SSlzdHVkZW50M0c2Ig==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1004" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10"><Font italic="true">Printing records</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1000" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Before going any further, take a look at the current state of <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords</Font>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L1001" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">studentRecords;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">N2VuIiIhSSlzdHVkZW50Mkc2IkYjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0kpc3R1ZGVudDFHRiVJKXN0dWRlbnQzR0YlRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGIw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1003" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">This isn't very informative since it only displays the name of the table in each location, but not the data.  We need to write a procedure to print out the data.  To do this, we loop through the entries of the list and, for those that are non-zero, print the index, and the data from the table stored in that position.  Recall that the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:indices" hyperlink="true"><Font style="Maple Input" underline="true" executable="false">entries</Font></Hyperlink> command applied to a table returns the data stored in the table.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L1002" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">PrintRecords := proc()
  local i;
  global studentRecords;
  for i from 1 to 57 do
    if studentRecords[i] &lt;&gt; 0 then
      print(i,entries(studentRecords[i]));
    end if;
  end do;
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L999" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">PrintRecords();</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NiUiIiM3IyQiJCpHISIjNyMiJTNI</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NiUiI0M3IyQiJEAkISIjNyMiJT50</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NiUiI0Q3IyQiJFUkISIjNyMiJXls</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L993" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10"><Font italic="true">A procedure for storing new records</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L519" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now we'll write a procedure <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Store</Font> to automate this process.  <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Store</Font> will accept two arguments, the ID and GPA of a student, and will add that student's record to the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords</Font> list (database).</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L520" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">The first step in implementing <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Store</Font> will be to assign to a local variable, which we'll call <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">record</Font>, the table representing the student record.  Then <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Store</Font> needs to determine the location in the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords</Font> list in which the record will be stored.  In particular, it will need to avoid collision.  To do this, we'll use something similar to the linear probing function defined in the text.  Beginning with <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, we'll calculate <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.  We will store that value in the local name <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">hash</Font> and check to see if <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords[hash]</Font> is 0.  If so, then we know the list does not already have a record stored in that location and we can stop our search for an open position.  Otherwise, we increment <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiaUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEiaUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> and continue looking.  Once we have found an open position, we only need to assign our <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">record</Font> to that position.  We give <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">return NULL;</Font> as the final command so that the procedure does not display anything when the record is successfully stored.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L995" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Note that for this procedure we chose not to include the database as a parameter, but instead we've described the procedure in relation to the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords</Font> list that we began above.  This can result in a significant improvement in performance, especially when the list of records is long, because the database does not have to be passed as an argument to the procedure and then returned from it each time a new record is to be stored.  The disadvantage, of course, is that in order to use a different name for the database, we have to revise the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Store</Font> procedure.  </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L521" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">In order to use <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords</Font>, it must be declared in the procedure as a global variable.  This is done immediately after the local variables are declared with the keyword <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">global</Font>.  Without this declaration, Maple will assume that we forgot to list it as a local variable and and will treat the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords</Font> name inside the procedure as different from the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords</Font> list we created outside the procedure.  </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L524" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Here is the completed <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Store</Font> procedure.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L525" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Store := proc(id::integer,gpa::float)
  local hash, i, record;
  global studentRecords;
  record := table([&quot;ID&quot;=id,&quot;GPA&quot;=gpa]);
  for i from 0 to 56 do
    hash := calculateHash(id + i);
    if studentRecords[hash] = 0 then
      break;
    end if;
  end do;
  studentRecords[hash] := record;
  return NULL;
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L534" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Now we'll add a few records.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L535" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Store(2216,1.98);</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" labelreference="L536" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Store(1325,3.14);</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" labelreference="L537" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Store(7061,3.51);</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L539" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Look again at <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords</Font>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L540" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">studentRecords;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">N2VuIiIhSSlzdHVkZW50Mkc2IkYjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0kncmVjb3JkR0YlRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0kpc3R1ZGVudDFHRiVJKXN0dWRlbnQzR0YlRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGI0YjRiNGJkYmRiNGI0YjRiNGIw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L542" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Note that the three records we just added all appear as &quot;record&quot; in the list.  This is because <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">record</Font> was the name we used in the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Store</Font> procedure.  The <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">PrintRecords</Font> procedure shows us, however, that despite having the same names, they store the correct information.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group view="code" labelreference="L543" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">PrintRecords();</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NiUiIiM3IyQiJCpHISIjNyMiJTNI</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NiUiIzo3IyQiJDkkISIjNyMiJUQ4</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NiUiI0M3IyQiJEAkISIjNyMiJT50</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NiUiI0Q3IyQiJFUkISIjNyMiJXls</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NiUiI143IyQiJCk+ISIjNyMiJTtB</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output">NiUiI183IyQiJF4kISIjNyMiJWhx</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L545" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Because <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">record</Font> was declared as local within <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Store</Font>, Maple considers each one to be a distinct table, even though they have the same name.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1006" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10"><Font italic="true">Retrieving records</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L546" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font encoding="UTF-8">We now have procedures for storing a student record in our database and for printing all of the records.  But we also need a way to retrieve the record for a particular student.  Indeed, one of the benefits of hash functions is that they provide an efficient way to look up records \342\200\224 given the unique key, we need only apply the hash function to determine the memory location in which the record is stored (subject to collision of course).</Font></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L1008" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Our <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Retrieve</Font> procedure will accept a student ID number as its input and return the table storing the students record.  Most of the work will take place within the same for loop as was in the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Store</Font> procedure.  We first test to make sure the location we're looking in is non-zero.  If the location is 0, that tells us that the entry does not exist and the procedure will return <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">FAIL</Font>.  </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L547" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">Assuming the location is not 0, we check to see if the ID of the record in that position is the ID we're looking for.  If so, we return the table by applying <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:eval" hyperlink="true"><Font style="Maple Input" underline="true" executable="false">eval</Font></Hyperlink> to the entry in <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">studentRecords</Font>.  (Without the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:eval" hyperlink="true"><Font style="Maple Input" underline="true" executable="false">eval</Font></Hyperlink>, the procedure would return the name of the table rather than the table itself.)  If the ID is not the one we're searching for, it must have been the case that our record was pushed down the line because of a collision and we continue the loop.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group autoexecute="true" view="code" labelreference="L548" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Retrieve := proc(id::integer)
  local hash, i;
  global studentRecords;
  for i from 0 to 56 do
    hash := calculateHash(id + i);
    if studentRecords[hash] = 0 then
      return FAIL;
    end if;
    if studentRecords[hash][&quot;ID&quot;] = id then
      return eval(studentRecords[hash]);
    end if;
  end do;
  return FAIL;
end proc:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L549" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Retrieve(1325);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output>
<Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">PTYiSSZmYWxzZUclKnByb3RlY3RlZEdFXFtsI1EkR1BBRiMkIiQ5JCEiI1EjSURGIyIlRDg=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
