<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L785" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Font bold="true">Exercise 1.</Font>  Test which is faster for computing the greatest common divisor of a collection of integers, the <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:igcd" hyperlink="true"><Font style="Maple Input" underline="true" executable="false">igcd</Font></Hyperlink> or <Hyperlink linktarget="Help:gcd" hyperlink="true"><Font style="Maple Input" underline="true" executable="false">gcd</Font></Hyperlink> command.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L786" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10"><Font bold="true">Exercise 2.</Font>  Use Maple to generate the list of the first 100 prime numbers larger than one million.</Text-field>
